+
+## Hide and delete from the dashboard (Agents & sessions > Memory > Sessions)
+
+Installed by `MONI_AI_OS/deploy/claude-memory-manage/install.sh` (backup, `migrate.sql`, this patch,
+restart). The dashboard writes through `moni-helper` (`cc-mm-*`, root via sudo, bridge as `claude_mem`),
+permission `claude.memory.manage`, audited with counts only.
+
+| | Fact | Chunk |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Hide** (reversible) | `superseded_by = id` + `meta.forgotten_via = dashboard` (same as `memory_forget`) | `chunks.hidden = true` |
+| **Unhide** | `superseded_by = NULL`, retraction keys removed | `hidden = false` |
+| **Delete** | row deleted; older versions re-pointed to the surviving newer one, else hidden | row deleted + `memory_tombstones(content_hash)` |
+| **Delete session** | all its facts | all its chunks, its `ingest_state` rows (`<sid>.jsonl`, `<sid>/subagents/*`, `facts:<sid>`), and a row in `excluded_sessions` |
+
+Every read skips hidden chunks: `/search` (both chunk lists), the MCP keyword fallback,
+`memory_session` (`session_chunks`), fact extraction and `pending_sessions`, and the dashboard graph.
+`ingest.py` skips files of an excluded session (checked after taking the per-path lock) and never
+re-creates a tombstoned chunk; an upsert never touches `hidden`, so a hidden chunk stays hidden when
+its still-growing exchange is re-read. A full rebuild (truncate chunks + clear ingest_state) keeps
+exclusions and tombstones but loses `hidden` flags. Nightly dumps keep deleted rows until they rotate.
+`CLAUDE_MEMORY_SERVICE` (hooks, MCP) and `CLAUDE_MEMORY_HOOK_LOG` (hooks) exist for tests only.
